# Whitelist approach: ignore everything, then re-admit only what the repo
# should carry. A new working directory dropped into the project therefore
# stays out by default instead of being published by accident.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/index.html
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/LICENSE.txt
!/THIRD-PARTY.txt
!/css/
!/img/
!/js/

# Deliberately excluded, and why:
#   _altirra/      full Altirra source (29 MB), kept locally as reference only
#   _disks/        69 MB of test images, including commercial games
#   documentation/ third-party PDF manuals (LiteDOS, MyDOS, SpartaDOS X)
#   _doc/          source of README.md, kept local to avoid two copies
#   _tests/        Node test harness; needs _disks/ to run
#   _temp/         scratch space
#   app.md         private project notes
#   .agents/ .claude/ .vscode/  local tooling configuration

# Editor and OS noise, in case any of the published directories collect it.
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
